Z||000000||fropuff||12-06-2000||08:45 PM||||Hey, I decided to make my own side scoop out of fiberglass for a spare quarter panel that I got from 2M4 Dale.  I already planned it out and made a "mold" out of cardboard, and I have a question:  on the rear of the scoop, the rear facing the rear tire, I was wondering if I should leave a small gap for the air to escape out of.  It's only about a 1/16" gap, and I don't know if I should put it in there or not.  I know that some of the air would escape, but I don't know if this is better than sealing it off.  I would think that sealing it off would make it fly off or break, even though it would be glassed in or something like that.  Thanks for the answers.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
